description.content:
Get all appointments for a client.

## Response
Returns an array of appointments. If the client has no appointments, returns an empty array `[]`.

### Array Item Structure
Each item in the array has the following structure:
```typescript
{
  id: string;                    // Appointment UUID
  appointment_time: string;     // ISO 8601 timestamp
  service_type: string;         // Service type (e.g., 'Consultation', 'Surgery')
  status: string;               // Appointment status (e.g., 'scheduled', 'completed')
  payment_status: string;       // Payment status (e.g., 'pending', 'paid')
  symptoms: string | null;      // Symptoms (optional)
  notes: string | null;         // Notes (optional)
  client_notes: string | null; // Client notes (optional)
  reason_for_consultation: string | null; // Reason (optional)
  estimated_duration: number | null; // Duration in minutes (optional)
  emergency_level: string | null; // Emergency level (optional)
  is_telehealth: boolean;      // Whether it's a telehealth appointment
  pet_id: string | null;        // Pet UUID (optional)
  client_id: string;           // Client UUID
  vet_id: string | null;       // Veterinarian UUID (optional)
  tenant_id: string;           // Clinic UUID
  created_at: string;           // ISO 8601 timestamp
  updated_at: string;           // ISO 8601 timestamp
  pets: {                       // Pet details (nested object, if pet_id exists)
    id: string;
    name: string;
    species: string;
    breed: string | null;
    clients: {
      id: string;
      phone: string | null;
      users: {
        id: string;
        full_name: string;
        email: string;
      } | null;
    } | null;
  } | null;
  users: {                      // Veterinarian details (nested object, if vet_id exists)
    id: string;
    full_name: string;
  } | null;
}
```

Retrieve all pets. If clinicId query parameter is provided, filters by clinic. Otherwise returns pets for authenticated user's clinic.

The first pet ID will be automatically extracted and stored in the `pet_id` environment variable for use in other pet requests.

## Response
Returns an array of pets. If no pets are found, returns an empty array `[]`.

### Array Item Structure
Each item in the array has the following structure:
```typescript
{
  id: string;                    // Pet UUID
  name: string;                 // Pet name
  species: string;              // Pet species (e.g., 'Dog', 'Cat')
  breed: string | null;         // Pet breed (optional)
  birth_date: string | null;    // ISO 8601 date (optional)
  weight: number | null;        // Pet weight (optional)
  gender: string | null;        // Pet gender (optional)
  allergies: string | null;    // Pet allergies (optional)
  client_id: string;           // Client UUID (owner)
  tenant_id: string;           // Clinic UUID
  created_at: string;           // ISO 8601 timestamp
  updated_at: string;          // ISO 8601 timestamp
  clients: {                    // Client details (nested object)
    id: string;
    user_id: string;
    users: {
      id: string;
      email: string;
      full_name: string;
    } | null;
  } | null;
  // ... other fields from pets table
}
```

Get all users for the authenticated user's organization/clinic. User IDs are automatically extracted and stored for use in "Bulk Delete Users" and "Bulk Update Users" endpoints.

## Response
Returns an array of users. If no users are found, returns an empty array `[]`.

### Array Item Structure
Each item in the array has the following structure:
```typescript
{
  id: string;                    // User UUID (from users table)
  auth_user_id: string;          // Supabase auth user ID
  email: string;                 // User email
  full_name: string;             // User's full name
  first_name: string;           // User's first name
  last_name: string;            // User's last name
  role: string;                  // User role (e.g., 'veterinarian', 'clinic_admin')
  role_id: string | null;        // Custom role ID (if applicable)
  role_name: string | null;      // Custom role name (if applicable)
  organization_id: string;       // Organization UUID
  clinic_id: string;            // Clinic UUID
  status: string;               // User status (e.g., 'active', 'inactive')
  created_at: string;            // ISO 8601 timestamp
  has_set_password: boolean;    // Whether user has set a password
  organizations: {               // Organization details (nested object)
    id: string;
    name: string;
  } | null;
  clinics: {                     // Clinic details (nested object)
    id: string;
    name: string;
  } | null;
}
```

Get services for a clinic, optionally filtered by active status. The first service ID from the response is automatically stored in `service_id` environment variable for use in Update Clinic Service endpoint.

## Response
Returns an array of clinic services/products. If the clinic has no services, returns an empty array `[]`.

### Array Item Structure
Each item in the array has the following structure:
```typescript
{
  id: string;                          // Service UUID
  clinic_id: string;                   // Clinic UUID
  service_name: string;                // Name of the service/product
  default_medical_record_note?: string | null;
  description: string;                 // Service description
  duration_minutes: number;            // Duration in minutes
  price: number;                       // Service price
  is_active: boolean;                  // Whether the service is active
  created_at: string;                  // ISO 8601 timestamp
  updated_at: string;                  // ISO 8601 timestamp
  type: 'Injections' | 'Medication' | 'Product' | 'Service' | 'Vaccine';
  details: object;                     // Type-specific details (varies by type)
  include_in_medical_record: boolean;
  include_on_invoice_if_declined: boolean;
  invoice_line_name: string;
  inventory_id: string;
  price_setting: {                      // Price settings object
    selling_price: number;
    min_price: number;
    dispensing_fee_id?: string | null;
    dispensing_fee_amt: number;
    include_on_estimate_and_invoice_print: boolean;
    client_discount_eligible: boolean;
    hide_from_treatment_search: boolean;
    default_product_discount: boolean;
    taxable: boolean;
    discount?: { type: '%' | '$'; discount: number; note: string; } | null;
  };
  automatic_actions: {                 // Automatic task settings
    title: string;
    due_in: number;
    time_unit: 'Day(s)' | 'Week(s)' | 'Months(s)' | 'Year(s)';
    assigned_user_id: string | null;
    priority: 'Low' | 'Medium' | 'Urgent';
  } | null;
  discharge_instructions: string | null;
  category_id: string | null;
  dispensing_id: string | null;
  productLots?: Array<{                // Optional product lots
    id?: string;
    created_at?: string;
    clinic_service_id?: string;
    manufacturer: string;
    serial_number: string;
    lot_number: string;
    expiration_date: string;
    bottle_number: string | null;
  }>;
}
```

